{"demo_id": "10003_2105_14444.txt::sent::92", "doc_id": "10003_2105_14444.txt", "context_type": "sentence", "sent_idx": 111, "context_text": "We compare our NAS-BERT models with hand-designed BERT models under the same parameter size and latency (denoted as BERT 60, BERT 30, BERT 10 and BERT 5 We mainly compare our NAS-BERT with methods whose teacher model is BERT base for a fair comparison including 1) DistilBERT [37], which uses knowledge distillation on the pre-training stage; 2) BERT-PKD [41], which distills the knowledge from the intermediate layers and the final output logits on the pre-training stage; 3) BERT-of-Theseus [53], which uses module replacement for compression; 4) MiniLM [49], which transfers the knowledge from the self-attention module; 5) PD-BERT [44], which distills the knowledge from the target domain in BERT training; 6) DynaBERT [16], which uses network rewiring to adjust width and depth of BERT for each downstream task.", "entities": [{"text": "NAS-BERT", "start_token": 3977, "end_token": 3979, "start_char": 20580, "end_char": 20588, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "BERT", "start_token": 3985, "end_token": 3985, "start_char": 20615, "end_char": 20619, "ner_label": "ModelArchitecture"}, {"text": "BERT 60", "start_token": 3997, "end_token": 3998, "start_char": 20681, "end_char": 20688, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "BERT 30", "start_token": 4000, "end_token": 4001, "start_char": 20691, "end_char": 20698, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "BERT 10", "start_token": 4003, "end_token": 4004, "start_char": 20701, "end_char": 20708, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "BERT 5", "start_token": 4006, "end_token": 4007, "start_char": 20713, "end_char": 20719, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "NAS-BERT", "start_token": 4012, "end_token": 4014, "start_char": 20742, "end_char": 20750, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "BERT base", "start_token": 4021, "end_token": 4022, "start_char": 20787, "end_char": 20796, "ner_label": "ModelArchitecture"}, {"text